  "ownership": "One input/keyboard admission funds one original async worker, blocking X11 worker and connection. Two owned names each limited to 4096 bytes; fixed nine-element matrix. Lookup and write use the same connection; ambiguity rejects before write. Original request check distinguishes X11 errors from transport loss. Connection drops inside blocking worker before its join; operation joins before reuse. Cancellation/deadline does not drop original work; genuine unknown stays owned. No resource-to-owner cycle or input-payload borrow escapes. x11rb 0.13.2 connect rejects invalid screen indexes before returning.",
  "bounds": "All 65536 orientation flag values and all 16 valid rotation/reflection combinations tested. Existing xinput 1.6.4 transform behavior independently implemented by corner composition. Geometry rejects zero dimensions; matrix is fixed-size call-owned output.",
  "checks": "Rust format, diff whitespace, production cargo check with accessory-transport pass. 26/26 maintained methods >=82.14% line coverage; 116/116 measured functions complexity <=9. Rust 1.100.0, cargo-llvm-cov 0.8.7, project syn 2.0.119 complexity checker. CI installs xinput for private X11 fixtures.",
  "limits": "Private Xvfb and D-Bus only; no installed Blent, physical input device, live KWin property, ADB or USB session changed. Does not prove atomicity against arbitrary registry replacement between name lookup and effect."
